You’re at the point where each package needs its own mini‑PRD: scope, goals, non‑goals, and milestones that hang off the overall product. I’ll outline those next.

Below I’ll keep them concise but concrete so you can implement or RFC them package by package.

1. @melon/db – core engine
Scope
Schema/model metadata.

Internal query AST and planning.

Storage adapter contract.

MelonDatabase / MelonCollection / query handles.

Transactions, read/write coordination, subscriptions.

WatermelonDB’s Database + DatabaseAdapter + Collection responsibilities all live here, but with a single AST and TypeScript-first design.

Goals
Provide a database-agnostic core: adapters translate AST → storage operations.

Preserve lazy, local-first, reactive behavior that WatermelonDB uses for large RN apps.

Be fully TypeScript typed and React-agnostic.

Non‑goals
No direct React APIs.

No Prisma/Mango parsing here (only AST types).

No sync in this package.

Requirements
Schema: DatabaseSchemaDefinition, CollectionSchemaDefinition, relation metadata.

AST: QueryAst, QueryBooleanNode, QueryPlan, PreparedQuery.

Adapter: StorageAdapter with initialize, find, count, write, transaction, observeQuery?.

Runtime: MelonDatabase, MelonCollection, MelonQueryHandle, read/write contexts.

Observability: collection-level change signals.

Milestones
M0 – Core design (1–2 weeks)

Finalize schema types, AST shape, adapter interface.

Validate against WatermelonDB adapter docs and architecture.

M1 – In-memory adapter + engine alpha (2–3 weeks)

Implement MelonDatabase, MelonCollection, in-memory StorageAdapter.

CRUD and basic queries via AST.

Unit tests and simple benchmarks.

M2 – SQLite adapter integration contract (2 weeks)

Finalize hooks for @melon/db-sqlite (e.g., SQL generation inputs).

Stabilize AST for v1.

2. @melon/db-sqlite – SQLite adapter
Scope
Production StorageAdapter implementation for SQLite on RN (JSI / new arch) and Node.

WatermelonDB’s main performance story is “lazy, SQLite-backed, separate thread,” so this package is critical.

Goals
Provide a performant SQLite adapter that consumes PreparedQuery and write ops.

Support RN new architecture integration pattern.

Support basic observability (query timing, change subscriptions).

Non‑goals
No query parsing.

No schema migration planner (schema comes from @melon/db).

Requirements
createSqliteAdapter({ filename, jsi, debug }): StorageAdapter.

Compile QueryAst → SQL (SELECT, COUNT, JOIN) with safe parameterization.

Implement transaction and observeQuery to support reactive queries and writer semantics.

Support RN new arch: JSI/TurboModule, documented setup.

Milestones
M0 – SQL generator (2–3 weeks)

Map AST filter/sort/limit → SQL subset.

Tests covering simple and compound queries.

M1 – RN/Node adapter alpha (3–4 weeks)

Implement adapter methods, backed by SQLite.

Basic RN new-arch binding with one demo app.

M2 – Perf & stability (3 weeks)

Benchmarks on realistic datasets.

Stress tests for transactions and subscriptions.

3. @melon/db-query – fluent query builder
Scope
Type-safe fluent query builder → QueryAst.

Utilities for common patterns (whereEq, byId, byForeignKey).

Goals
Be the canonical in-repo query surface.

Keep APIs functional and composable (pure builders, no side effects).

Non‑goals
No direct DB access; returns AST only.

No schema import (schema comes from @melon/db).

Requirements
QueryBuilder<Record> with where, and, or, orderBy, limit, skip, include, toAst.

createQueryFactory(schema: MelonSchema): QueryFactory.

Good TS inference for field names and relations.

Milestones
M0 – API RFC (1 week)

Lock down builder ergonomics.

Compare to current WatermelonDB query ergonomics for migration friendliness.

M1 – Builder implementation (2–3 weeks)

Implement builder + tests for AST output.

Docs with examples.

4. @melon/db-query-mango – Mango query language
Scope
Mango-style JSON query language parser/validator → AST.

Support a well-defined subset of Mango (RxDB/CouchDB style).

Goals
Provide a serializable query DSL for configs, tests, devtools.

Align semantics with Mango/RxDB for familiarity, but with explicit support matrix.

Non‑goals
Full CouchDB Mango parity in v1.

Network/remote execution (local-only).

Requirements
MangoQuery { selector, sort, skip, limit, fields? }.

MangoQueryCompiler → PreparedQuery.

Clear error messages for unsupported operators.

Docs mapping Mango → supported AST.

Milestones
M0 – Supported subset design (1 week)

Decide operators: equality, comparisons, and/or, sort, skip/limit.

M1 – Parser/compiler alpha (2–3 weeks)

Implement normalization + compilation to AST.

Tests using sample RxDB-like queries.

5. @melon/db-prisma – Prisma schema & client
Scope
Prisma schema import → DatabaseSchemaDefinition.

Codegen for TS types and Prisma-like local client facades.

Goals
Let teams reuse Prisma-like schemas and client ergonomics locally.

Integrate smoothly with Bun workspaces (Prisma + Bun is already documented).

Non‑goals
Running full Prisma engine in RN; this is a compatibility layer, not a full Prisma runtime.

Remote DB management (handled separately if desired).

Requirements
PrismaSchemaImporter.importSchema(prismaSchema: string): DatabaseSchemaDefinition.

Codegen CLI: generate TS types, PrismaLikeClient, and optional hooks.

createPrismaLikeClient(db: MelonDatabase): PrismaLikeClient.

Milestones
M0 – Schema + Bun/Prisma integration design (1–2 weeks)

Leverage Prisma + Bun guidance for monorepos.

Decide subset of Prisma schema to support.

M1 – Import + codegen alpha (3–4 weeks)

Parse schema → DatabaseSchemaDefinition.

Generate type-safe clients and basic queries mapping to AST.

6. @melon/db-react – React bindings
Scope
React context + hooks around MelonDatabase and PreparedQuery.

Ergonomics similar to WatermelonDB’s provider/hooks and Prisma’s RN reactive queries.

Goals
Minimal overhead; just wire subscriptions to React.

Hooks-first API (useDatabase, useCollection, useQuery, useWriter).

Non‑goals
No schema or adapter logic.

No devtools UI here (that’s in devtools).

Requirements
<MelonDbProvider db> using React context (like WatermelonDB’s DatabaseProvider).

Hooks as sketched earlier.

Good SSR behavior for docs/web (if needed).

Milestones
M0 – Hook API design (1 week)

Nail the surface inspired by WatermelonDB hooks and Prisma RN docs.

M1 – Implementation + example (2–3 weeks)

Use in apps/playground-rn.

Document patterns.

7. @melon/db-devtools – devtools
Scope
Bridge to capture AST, SQL, timings, errors.

Optional UI panel (web and possibly RN).

Goals
Make multi-surface queries debuggable (fluent, Prisma, Mango).

Zero-cost when disabled.

Non‑goals
No core logic or adapters.

Requirements
DevtoolsBridge interface and a simple default implementation.

Overlay/panel integrated into apps/playground-*.

Milestones
M0 – Debug event design (1 week)

M1 – Bridge + minimal panel (2–3 weeks)

8. @melon/db-testkit – test utilities
Scope
In-memory adapter.

Helpers for creating and tearing down test databases.

Goals
Make it easy to test without RN/native SQLite.

Encourage pure, deterministic tests.

Non‑goals
No heavy mocking of React; this is DB-level.

Requirements
createInMemoryAdapter().

withTestDatabase(schema, fn) helper.

Milestones
M0 – In-memory adapter (1–2 weeks)

M1 – Helpers and examples (1–2 weeks)

9. @melon/db-codemods – migration
Scope
Codemods and compatibility helpers to move from WatermelonDB.

Goals
Lower migration friction.

Focus on common patterns first.

Non‑goals
100% automated migration for every edge case.

Requirements
CLI codemods for database.get().query() & writer patterns.

Mapping Watermelon query descriptors → new AST.

Milestones
M0 – Compatibility matrix (1–2 weeks)

M1 – Codemods for top 3–5 patterns (2–3 weeks)